---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const updated = '17 October 2026';
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy — FreeSense" description="How freesense.org handles your data: no tracking, no advertising cookies, minimal essential storage.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <span class="eyebrow reveal">Legal</span>
      <h1 class="reveal d1">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="small-note reveal d1">Last updated: {updated}</p>
      <p class="lead-muted reveal d2">
        FreeSense respects your privacy. <strong>freesense.org</strong> is a static website with no user accounts, no advertising
        and no cross-site tracking. This page explains the little data that is involved when you visit.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-page" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <div class="fs-card">
        <h2 class="mt-0" style="font-size:1.3rem">The short version</h2>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li><span>No advertising or tracking cookies, and no analytics that profile you.</span></li>
          <li><span>The only browser storage is your own colour-theme choice.</span></li>
          <li><span>Fonts and scripts are served from this site; no third-party CDNs.</span></li>
          <li><span>The installed firewall sends no telemetry, device ID or configuration to us.</span></li>
          <li><span>We never sell or share personal data; we do not collect any to begin with.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>This site is operated by <strong>The FreeSense Project</strong>, an open-source community project. For privacy questions, contact us via the <a href="https://github.com/FreeSense-org" rel="noopener">FreeSense-org GitHub organization</a>.</p>

      <h2>2. Cookies &amp; local storage</h2>
      <p>We do not set cookies. The site stores a single value in your browser's <code>localStorage</code>, <code>fs-theme</code>, which remembers whether you chose the light, dark or system colour theme. It contains no personal information and is never sent to a server. You can clear it any time in your browser settings.</p>

      <h2>3. Server logs (hosting)</h2>
      <p>The website, package service and download images are served by <strong>Cloudflare</strong> (Pages and R2). As part of delivering and protecting them, Cloudflare processes standard request metadata such as your IP address, browser user-agent and the page or file requested. This is used only for operating the service, security and abuse prevention, under Cloudflare's own privacy terms. We do not combine it with anything else or use it to identify you.</p>

      <h2>4. Third-party requests</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Releases and updates</strong>: the website reads public release documents from <code>pkg.freesense.org</code> and recent commits and app releases from the public GitHub API, through this site's own server. Installer images are served by <code>downloads.freesense.org</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>GitHub</strong>: links to source code and issues take you to github.com, which has its own privacy policy.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Installed FreeSense systems</h2>
      <p>FreeSense contains no project telemetry, device registration, automatic configuration upload or usage reporting. The updater makes unauthenticated HTTPS requests to <code>pkg.freesense.org</code> for a signed repository manifest, update notes, repository metadata and packages. Network services and optional packages you enable may contact the upstream services you configure; those connections are separate from FreeSense project telemetry.</p>

      <h2>6. What we do not do</h2>
      <p>We do not run advertising networks, social-media trackers, session recording or fingerprinting. We do not create user profiles. We do not sell, rent or share personal data.</p>

      <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
      <p>If you are in the EU/EEA or UK, the GDPR gives you rights to access, correct or erase personal data and to object to processing. Because this site does not collect or store personal data beyond the transient server logs described above, there is normally nothing to retrieve, but you are welcome to contact us with any request or question.</p>

      <h2>8. Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy as the site evolves. Material changes are reflected by the &ldquo;last updated&rdquo; date above.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
